concept concept {
  name     = "Concept"
  summary  = "A unit that captures an idea or mental model the reader must grasp — a sharp summary plus a wdoc body, rendered to its own page and cross-linked to related units."
  related  = [entity, fact, process, datapresentation]
  body {
    p <<BODY
A concept is one of the wskill model's interlinking units. Use it for an idea, a
mechanism, or a way of thinking about the topic — something the reader needs to
understand rather than look up. It is a thin record: a `name` (the headline and link
text) and a `summary` (a one-liner that feeds the SKILL.md concept index), plus an
addressable `body` of paragraphs, tables, code and links that rides on the record and
is projected onto its own page. The `related` field lists other unit ids of any kind, which the
templates resolve to links — so concepts, entities, facts and processes all
cross-reference each other.
BODY
  }
}
